{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-61-1","title":"Isaiah 61:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The office of Christ. 4 The forwardness; 7 and blessing of the faithful.</p>\n<p>Spirit. 11:2-5; 42:1; 59:21; Mt 3:16; Lu 4:18,19; Joh 1:32,33; 3:34 anointed. Ps 2:6; *marg: Ps 45:7; Da 9:24; Joh 1:41; Ac 4:27; 10:38; Heb 1:9 to preach. 52:9; Ps 22:26; 25:9; 69:32; 149:4; Mt 5:3-5; 11:5; Lu 7:22 to bind. 57:15; 66:2; Ps 34:18; 51:17; 147:3; Ho 6:1; 2Co 7:6 to proclaim.The proclaiming of perfect liberty to the bound, and the year of acceptance with Jehovah, is a manifest allusion to the proclaiming of the year of the jubilee by sound of trumpet; and our Saviour, by applying this text to himself, plainly declares the typical design of that institution.</p>\n<p>42:7; 49:9,24,25; Ps 102:20; Jer 34:8; Zec 9:11,12; Joh 8:32-36 Ac 26:18; Ro 6:16-22; 7:23-25; 2Ti 2:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-2","title":"Isaiah 61:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the acceptable. Le 25:9-13; Lu 4:19; 2Co 6:2 and. 34:8; 35:4; 59:17,18; 63:1-6; 66:14; Ps 110:5,6; Jer 46:10 Mal 4:1-3; Lu 21:22-24; 1Th 2:16; 2Th 1:7-9 to comfort. 25:8; 57:18; 66:10-12; Jer 31:13; Mt 5:4; Lu 6:21; 7:44-50 Joh 16:20-22; 2Co 1:4,5; 2Th 2:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-3","title":"Isaiah 61:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>beauty. 12:1; Es 4:1-3; 8:15; 9:22; Ps 30:11; Eze 16:8-13 the oil. Ps 23:5; 45:7; 104:15; Ec 9:8; Joh 16:20 the garment. 10; Zec 3:5; Lu 15:22; Re 7:9-14 called. 60:21; Ps 92:12-15; Jer 17:7,8; Mt 7:17-19 that he. Mt 5:16; Joh 15:8; 1Co 6:20; Php 1:11; 2Th 1:10; 1Pe 2:9; 4:9-11,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-4","title":"Isaiah 61:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>49:6-8; 58:12; Eze 36:23-26,33-36; Am 9:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-5","title":"Isaiah 61:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>14:1,2; 60:10-14; Eph 2:12-20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-6","title":"Isaiah 61:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>named. 60:17; 66:21; Ex 19:6; Ro 12:1; 1Pe 2:5,9; Re 1:6; 5:10; 20:6 called. Eze 14:11; 1Co 3:5; 4:1; 2Co 6:4; 11:23; Eph 4:11,12 ye shall eat. 23:18; 60:5-7,10,11,16; 66:12; Ac 11:28-30; Ro 15:26,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-7","title":"Isaiah 61:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>your shame. 40:2; De 21:17; 2Ki 2:9; Job 42:10; Zec 9:12; 2Co 4:17 everlasting. 35:10; 51:11; 60:19,20; Ps 16:11; Mt 25:46; 2Th 2:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-8","title":"Isaiah 61:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I the Lord. Ps 11:7; 33:5; 37:28; 45:7; 99:4; Jer 9:24; Zec 8:16,17 I hate. 1:11-13; 1Sa 15:21-24; Jer 7:8-11; Am 5:21-24; Mt 23:14 I will direct. Ps 25:8-12; 32:8; Pr 3:6; 8:20; 2Th 3:5 I will make. 55:3; Ge 17:7; 2Sa 23:5; Ps 50:5; Jer 32:40; Heb 13:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-9","title":"Isaiah 61:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>their seed. 44:3; Ge 22:18; Zec 8:13; Ro 9:3,4 they are. 65:23; Ps 115:14; Ac 3:26; Ro 11:16-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-10","title":"Isaiah 61:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>will greatly. 35:10; 51:11; 1Sa 2:1; Ne 8:10; Ps 28:7; Hab 3:18; Zec 10:7 Lu 1:46,47; Ro 5:11; Php 3:1-3; 4:4; 1Pe 1:8; Re 19:7,8 for. 3; 52:1; 2Ch 6:41; Ps 132:9,16; Lu 15:22; Ro 3:22; 13:14; 14:17 Ga 3:27; Php 3:9; Re 4:4; 7:9-14; 21:2 as a. 49:18; Ps 45:8,9,13,14; Jer 2:32; Eze 16:8-16; Re 19:7,8; 21:2,9 decketh himself. Heb. decketh as a priest. Ex 28:2-43 with her. Ge 24:53</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-61-11","title":"Isaiah 61:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":61,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":61,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>as the earth. 55:10,11; 58:11; So 4:16; 5:1; Mt 13:3,8,23; Mr 4:26-32 so. 45:8; 62:1; Ps 72:3,16; 85:11 praises. 60:18; 62:7; 1Pe 2:9</p>"}]}